/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (Accomplishing government paperwork in India frequently turns out to be a complex process for many citizens due to the extensive and complex format of government forms, technical terminologies, overwhelming procedures, language barriers, physical accessibility challenges and low digital literacy particularly in rural areas complicating the task further. Digital automation using AI models practically simplifies this process, but current systems focus primarily on image-based, layout-based, agentic or Blackbox approaches, making them brittle, difficult to enhance and complex for edge deployments. Data scarcity is the most overwhelming factor that hampers the performance of current systems and their English centric design restricts their wide scale adaption in India. This project proposes the Governmental Form-Submissions via AI \(GovAI-Sub\) web application, integrating the Indic-Vision-ASR-NER AI \(IVAN AI\), an end-to-end novel solution to these problems in the form of a robust multilingual, multimodal, modular, light weight and easy to enhance system, employing Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\), Automatic Speech Recognition \(ASR\), Machine Translation and Named Entity Recognition \(NER\) to analyze and extract information from document images or speech and automatically populate the forms. GovAI-Sub and IVAN AI addresses critical gaps in existing research by providing an efficient and integrated multilingual solution specifically designed for Indian government forms with minimal data requirements. The system achieves 77.81% accuracy on hybrid Paddle-Surya OCR, 86.55% on customized Machine Translation using PolyGlot and Facebook nllb-200-distilled-600M, 92.33% on ASR with OpenAI Whisper Large-v3, and 79.8% on NER with BERT-Large. GovAI-Sub with the integration of IVAN AI reduces human errors, language barriers and manual effort, delivering a user-friendly and inclusive digital solution for improved citizen service accessibility and adaptability across India.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
