/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Problem Statement: These systemic barriers render government form-filling an arduous and error-prone process for average Indian citizens. The complexity is driven by lengthy structures, technical jargon, complex procedures, digital illiteracy and lack of clear instructions which frequently result in application rejections. While India is linguistically diverse, the reliance on English or Hindi-centric documentation necessitates that regional language speakers seek third-party assistance at cyber cafes or service centers incurring unnecessary costs and delays. Furthermore, manual data entry is plagued by illegible handwriting and incomplete submissions, leading to administrative bottlenecks and the potential denial of essential benefits. The absence of robust accessibility features and multilingual interfaces ultimately marginalizes aged and rural population or persons with disabilities, creating a significant disconnect between the current digital governance infrastructure and the goal of equitable service delivery.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Implemented Solution: To address these technical gaps, this project proposes the Indic-Vision-ASR-NER AI \(IVAN AI\), a modular, lightweight, easy to enhance, end-to-end multilingual and multimodal pipeline, along with the user friendly and easy-to-use Governmental Form-Submissions via AI \(GovAI-Sub\) web application Interface, designed for Indian government form automation. IVAN AI employs a dual-input architecture that supports document images or PDFs and voice-based input, ensuring accessibility for the elderly and users with motor, visual, vocal or auditory impairments. The document processing pipeline employs the IVAN-OCR, that utilizes a hybrid model combining the Paddle OCR [31] text detection module with the Surya OCR [36] text recognition module)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
