342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 223 0 R
/T (for robust Indic text extraction supporting 17 and 21 Indian languages respectively. These extracted code-mixed texts are processed by the IVAN-Translator, a customized integration of PolyGlot [44] and light-weight nllb-200-distilled-600M [38] supporting 11 and 22 Indian languages respectively to translate information into single high-resource English language from auto detected source language of the information. This strategy allows the use of IVAN-NER \(BERT-Doc-NER-Max\), a domain-adapted BERT-Large-NER model [59] fine-tuned on a custom English-centric text dataset of 21 government-specific entities including Aadhaar, PAN, pension details, etc., and is easily expandable to more types. By shifting from complex multilingual image-based extraction to an English-centric text-space post-OCR, the system reduces manual annotation overhead on images and improves generalization. For voice based interactions, the system employs the IVAN-ASR leveraging the OpenAI Whisper Large-v3 [42] to transcribe raw user speech, supporting 12 major Indic languages, followed by the IVAN-Translator for translating the ASR-transcribed text to a single target language. This real-time ASR-Translator pipeline auto-interprets spoken information, transcribing and translating relevant field information directly for form-filling, bypassing the need for explicit NER extraction. The GovAI-Sub web-app designed to integrate this IVAN AI pipeline is made with easy-accessibility and simplicity in mind, to cater to a large group of population across language, age, physical and other barriers. The interface is made simple and easy-to-use providing a clear set of instructions in user desired language in a digital platform, that is easily accessible from anywhere. Validated across 9 government document types and 3 synthetic forms, mimicking the structural complexity of actual government forms to ensure legal compliance, IVAN AI achieves 77.8% accuracy on OCR, 86.5% on Translation, 92.3% on ASR, and 79.8% on NER. The overall system of GovAI-Sub and IVAN AI remains lightweight and modular for edge deployment, effectively addressing the scalability and data scarcity challenges prevalent in current literature, while maintaining the multimodality, simplicity of form-filling process, lingual and accessibility concerns of existing manual and digital governance frameworks.)
/E (for robust Indic text extraction supporting 17 and 21 Indian languages respectively. These extracted code-mixed texts are processed by the IVAN-Translator, a customized integration of PolyGlot [44] and light-weight nllb-200-distilled-600M [38] supporting 11 and 22 Indian languages respectively to translate information into single high-resource English language from auto detected source language of the information. This strategy allows the use of IVAN-NER \(BERT-Doc-NER-Max\), a domain-adapted BERT-Large-NER model [59] fine-tuned on a custom English-centric text dataset of 21 government-specific entities including Aadhaar, PAN, pension details, etc., and is easily expandable to more types. By shifting from complex multilingual image-based extraction to an English-centric text-space post-OCR, the system reduces manual annotation overhead on images and improves generalization. For voice based interactions, the system employs the IVAN-ASR leveraging the OpenAI Whisper Large-v3 [42] to transcribe raw user speech, supporting 12 major Indic languages, followed by the IVAN-Translator for translating the ASR-transcribed text to a single target language. This real-time ASR-Translator pipeline auto-interprets spoken information, transcribing and translating relevant field information directly for form-filling, bypassing the need for explicit NER extraction. The GovAI-Sub web-app designed to integrate this IVAN AI pipeline is made with easy-accessibility and simplicity in mind, to cater to a large group of population across language, age, physical and other barriers. The interface is made simple and easy-to-use providing a clear set of instructions in user desired language in a digital platform, that is easily accessible from anywhere. Validated across 9 government document types and 3 synthetic forms, mimicking the structural complexity of actual government forms to ensure legal compliance, IVAN AI achieves 77.8% accuracy on OCR, 86.5% on Translation, 92.3% on ASR, and 79.8% on NER. The overall system of GovAI-Sub and IVAN AI remains lightweight and modular for edge deployment, effectively addressing the scalability and data scarcity challenges prevalent in current literature, while maintaining the multimodality, simplicity of form-filling process, lingual and accessibility concerns of existing manual and digital governance frameworks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
