509 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1696 0 R
/T (The ASR Module \(IVAN-ASR\): For voice modality, the OpenAI Whisper Large-v3 [39] was employed to process the uploaded Audio data from the User. Unlike standard implementations, the model was configured with the "transcribe" mode rather than direct "translate" mode. This design choice preserves the nuances of code-mixed Indic speech and efficiency of the ASR model, which are later processed by the IVAN-Translator. This ensures higher semantic fidelity for regional dialects and mixed-language inputs common in the Indian demographic.)
/E (The ASR Module \(IVAN-ASR\): For voice modality, the OpenAI Whisper Large-v3 [39] was employed to process the uploaded Audio data from the User. Unlike standard implementations, the model was configured with the "transcribe" mode rather than direct "translate" mode. This design choice preserves the nuances of code-mixed Indic speech and efficiency of the ASR model, which are later processed by the IVAN-Translator. This ensures higher semantic fidelity for regional dialects and mixed-language inputs common in the Indian demographic.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1697 0 R
/T (The Translator Module \(IVAN-Translator\): The translation module serves as a bridge to the simplified English-centric processing domain post-OCR and Indic form-filling post-ASR. The PolyGlot framework [37] was utilized for high-speed automatic language detection across code-mixed inputs. The detected source language\(s\) then gets passed to the Facebook nllb-200-distilled-600M [38] model along with the input text and target language for translation. The code-mixed text from OCR is translated to English \(if not already\) and transcribed ASR text is translated into the language selected by the user for form-filling using the IVAN-Translator module, serving as the key to simplify the handling of multilingual, code-mixed strings by translating them into a unified \(English or Indic\) text space. The "distilled" variant of NLLB was selected to maintain a lightweight footprint and repeated fallbacks in the pipeline.)
/E (The Translator Module \(IVAN-Translator\): The translation module serves as a bridge to the simplified English-centric processing domain post-OCR and Indic form-filling post-ASR. The PolyGlot framework [37] was utilized for high-speed automatic language detection across code-mixed inputs. The detected source language\(s\) then gets passed to the Facebook nllb-200-distilled-600M [38] model along with the input text and target language for translation. The code-mixed text from OCR is translated to English \(if not already\) and transcribed ASR text is translated into the language selected by the user for form-filling using the IVAN-Translator module, serving as the key to simplify the handling of multilingual, code-mixed strings by translating them into a unified \(English or Indic\) text space. The "distilled" variant of NLLB was selected to maintain a lightweight footprint and repeated fallbacks in the pipeline.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
