/P 1831 0 R
/T (The IVAN-OCR \(Hybrid DR OCR\) maintains improved performance at IR-based evaluation \(F1 Score\) with a zero-shot, lightweight-hybrid architecture showing its efficiency in retention of key information from documents during OCR. Furthermore, the processing latency of 3.46s per page with its ability to handle old-degraded documents, skewed, code-mixed, multilingual texts enables real-time deployment, offering a high-efficiency alternative to computationally expensive and layout-sensitive VLM-based or cloud-dependent pipelines.   )
/E (The IVAN-OCR \(Hybrid DR OCR\) maintains improved performance at IR-based evaluation \(F1 Score\) with a zero-shot, lightweight-hybrid architecture showing its efficiency in retention of key information from documents during OCR. Furthermore, the processing latency of 3.46s per page with its ability to handle old-degraded documents, skewed, code-mixed, multilingual texts enables real-time deployment, offering a high-efficiency alternative to computationally expensive and layout-sensitive VLM-based or cloud-dependent pipelines.   )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [16 17]
