1048 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (In Conclusion: This project presents the IVAN AI framework, integrable within the GovAI-Sub system, as a practical solution to India's digital governance challenges by enabling accessible, multilingual and multimodal automated form-filling for government services. Despite facing significant constraints from limited training data, legal restrictions on replicating government documents into a dataset with annotation complexities and various technical difficulties in developing IVAN AI pipelines on resource-limited environments, the system demonstrates considerable potential in bridging the digital divide for India's diverse population, with proved benchmarks. The hybrid approach of IVAN-OCR combining lightweight, zero-shot or few-shot models like PaddleOCR with robust engines like Surya-OCR for degraded documents, PolyGlot for language detection with NLLB-200 for translation and BERT-based entity extraction, alongside OpenAI Whisper for speech recognition effectively addresses the real-world complexities of Indian government forms featuring skewed layouts, multiple languages and varying document quality. While IVAN AI and GovAI-Sub integration was not successful due to computational constraints, the component-specific scores of the IVAN AI system and the successfully integrated end-to-end AI pipeline scores designed on those components mark significant progress and novelty in a domain where existing commercial solutions often fail on Indian systems due to their English-centric design, constrained resource environments or legal permissions. The easy-of-use, accessibility and adaptability focused design and development of the GovAI-Sub web interface also marks the significant mitigation of complex, time-consuming, manual governmental procedures, in the form of a fast-paced, digitalized platform.  The system can process both voice and document inputs \(dual-modality\) in 17-22 Indian languages, pull out important information from unclear OCR or ASR transcribed text and automatically fill the correct form fields. This makes it easier for elderly people, individuals with disabilities, low literacy rates and rural communities to access government services without struggling through complicated paperwork, increasing accessibility and adaptability.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0 1 2]
>>
endobj
